Stine,

Yes there is likely a difference. You should do this before the GPA. However, to figure out if there is a problem, you first do the GPA and PCA and plot. Then you identify the specimens to be reflected. Next you reflect them using their original coordinates and finally do a GPA of all specimens to align them after they are reflected to a common side.

Dean

